\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Exact population solutions on 200 preregistered cyclic games. ``Defined'' is the fraction for which the method returned a feasible policy, IR is the fraction strictly above the common fallback in every objective, and the Pareto gap is measured in the common game-value coordinates. MOPO uses objective 1 as primary and preregistered half-attainable thresholds. Methods optimize different social objectives, so the minimum surplus is diagnostic rather than a universal ranking.}}{20}{table.150}\protected@file@percent }
